<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Raymond of Poitiers</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1115–<a href="/years/1149">1149</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Raymond of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poitiers">Poitiers</a> was prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> from 1136 to 1149, a younger son of Duke William IX of Aquitaine who married the heiress Constance. In 1137 he had to accept the overlordship of the Byzantine emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-ii-komnenos">John II Komnenos</a>. He hosted his niece <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eleanor-of-aquitaine">Eleanor of Aquitaine</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-crusade">Second Crusade</a> and was killed fighting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nur-al-din">Nur al-Din</a> at the Battle of Inab.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/raymond-of-poitiers.jpg" alt="Raymond of Poitiers" width="289" height="401" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Raymond_of_Poitiers_with_John_II_Komnenos.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
